1.06 A. CONVERGENCE: 3x3x4 vs 3x3x5 differ by 0.001 eV. Coverage: 1/4 ML -4.904, 1/9 ML -4.837, 1/16 ML -4.845 eV. VALIDATION (same model/setup): Cu lattice constant 3.640 A vs exp 3.615 A (+0.7%, typical of PBE). Cu cohesive energy 3.50 eV vs exp 3.49 eV (textbook, Kittel). O2 binding 6.28 eV and bond 1.235 A, vs exp De ~5.2 eV: this is PBE-like overbinding of about 1.1 eV per O2, about 0.5 eV per O. The 1/4 ML fcc value (-4.90 eV) and fcc-hcp ordering match a PBE/VASP preprint found by web search (arXiv:2505.12914, as summarised by the search tool: fcc -5.00, hcp -4.905 eV vs gas-phase O). I did not read that paper myself, so treat it as a secondary check. UNCERTAINTY (0.5 eV, approximate): model error vs PBE about 0.1-0.15 eV; finite size/slab under 0.07 eV; atomic reference ambiguity up to about 0.5 eV. Combining E_ads(1/2 O2) = -1.69 eV with the experimental O2 De (about 5.21 eV) gives about -4.30 eV. So -4.84 eV is a PBE-level number; an experiment-scale estimate is about 0.5 eV weaker. No ZPE or thermal corrections are included; O ZPE on hollow sites is about 0.05-0.1 eV.\"\n },\n \"investigation_id\": \"\",\n \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-01T03:01:44.743897+00:00\",\n \"content_hash\": \"10a4956ee0c75c6423feb148609ab7d940b7aede3e64041e2bf74d6722caf26f\",\n \"parent_artifact_ids\": [\n  \"ff1090ba-e6d0-4bad-91a5-5499964be846\"\n ],\n \"result_quality\": \"ok\",\n \"needs\": [],\n \"summary\": \"O on Cu(111) adsorption_energy = -4.84 eV via ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (MACECalculator, float64, CUDA GB10)/MACE-MPA-0 medium (PBE/PBE+U-level universal MLIP) 0 K static: bulk Cu cell relaxed (a=3.640 A); fcc(111) slabs 2x2/3x3/4x4, 4-5 layers, 10 A vacuum each side, bottom half fixed; single O at fcc, hcp, bridge, top; BFGS fmax 0.01 eV/A. E_ads = E(O/slab) - E(slab) - E(O atom). O atom = single O in 15 A box (model's atomic reference energy). Reported value: fcc hollow, 3x3x4 (1/9 ML); 4x4x4 (1/16 ML) gives -4.845\"\n}\ncandidate:\n{\n \"additionalProperties\": false,